# CODEOWNERS — required reviewers per path (AGENTS.md golden rule 10:
# "Never break @edu/* without core-guardian"). On a protected `main`, GitHub blocks
# merge until a listed owner approves. This is the human half of the gate; CI is the
# automated half.
#
# RULES OF THIS FILE:
#  - The LAST matching pattern wins (NOT the most specific). Order general → specific.
#  - Owners must be real GitHub users WITH write access, else the rule is silently
#    ignored (a classic footgun). Today that's just the lead; extend as devs onboard.

# Default owner for anything not claimed below.
*                       @EdwardYCLui

# --- Shared core (@edu/*), apps, templates, scripts, city art: core-guardian gated.
# These are the split-freeze surfaces + the merge engine; a careless edit here breaks
# all 4 branches at once, which is exactly what core-guardian review prevents.
/packages/              @EdwardYCLui
/apps/                  @EdwardYCLui
/templates/             @EdwardYCLui
/scripts/               @EdwardYCLui
/city-art/              @EdwardYCLui
/.github/               @EdwardYCLui

# The contract is law (plan §3). Call it out explicitly so it's never accidentally
# folded into a broader, looser rule.
/packages/contract/     @EdwardYCLui

# Shared docs — the plan, progress tracker, and rules are core artifacts.
*.md                    @EdwardYCLui

# --- Games: owned by their authors, not core-guardian (games/<track>/<id>/**).
# Until the 4-way split is assigned, the lead owns these too. As devs join, append
# MORE-SPECIFIC lines AFTER this one so they win, e.g.:
#   /games/primary/waste-sorter/        @dev-c
#   /games/kindergarten/animal-sounds/  @dev-d
/games/                 @EdwardYCLui
